<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of Devolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1667">1667</a>–<a href="/years/1668">1668</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of Devolution was fought in 1667–1668 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> over the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> claimed parts of it for his wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a> under a local inheritance law, the 'right of devolution', and quickly overran much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> and Franche-Comté; alarmed, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/triple-alliance-1668">Triple Alliance</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> pressed for peace, and France kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lille">Lille</a> and other towns by the Treaty of Aix-la-Chapelle (1668).</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-devolution.jpg" alt="War of Devolution" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Baudouin Yvart / After Adam Frans van der Meulen / After Charles Le Brun · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LeBrun_Louis_XIV_at_Douai_in_the_War_of_Devolution_1667.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
